== gnucap modelgen tests

Run with "make check". Optionally TESTSELECT may be specified to subselect
tests

$ make check TESTSELECT=dump # will only run tests matching "dump*"

Desired output is stored in ref, actual output will be in check/*.out
See check/${TESTSELECT}.diffs for results (no diff == good).

Code coverage and status are reported during testing. If you are not
interested, redirect stderr, as in

$ make check 2>/dev/null

see below otherwise.

== Running single tests

Individual tests may be run directly in exactly the way "make check" does.
Normally, this involves some additional args and/or environment. To trigger
the run, regenerate the corresponding .out file.

$ make check/<test_file>.out

To also display the status, "regenerate" the .diff file, as in

$ make check/<test_file>.diff

Here, "pass", "fail" indicate match and mismatch with the reference
respectively. An empty diff will be deleted. "MISS" hints at the missing
reference.

== Code coverage testing

Test coverage is computed according to the following protocol, see [1] for
more background.

- Place "untested calls" at each test hook.
  There is an "untest" target in the top level Makefile.

- Compile the program with CPPFLAGS=-DTRACE_UNTESTED.

- Edit out the "untested" calls that are reached by the tests.

More automation is currently under test. The intent is to retest after every
change before committing.

[1] http://gnucap.org/dokuwiki/doku.php/gnucap:manual:tech:code_coverage_testing?s[]=testing
